WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.302
-President Trump and his allies
are freaking out

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.671
about a Democratic plan
to fight climate change.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:07.774
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.243
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:14.380
After Trump declared
a national emergency last week

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.714
to build a border wall,

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.184
he got some rare pushback
from members of his own party.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.386
But they weren't concerned

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.788
that Trump had made up
a fake emergency.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:24.224
They were concerned
that a Democratic president

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.925
could come along and use the law

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.528
to declare a real emergency
over climate change.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.830
-If you declare
a national emergency

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.332
to circumvent Congress
to pay for the border wall,

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:35.468
what's to stop
a liberal Democrat one day

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.837
from declaring climate change
as a national emergency?

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.438
-Maybe we're going to get
a Democratic president

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:40.773
and we're going to declare
a national emergency

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.141
on climate change.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:45.178
-If the President declares this
a national emergency,

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:48.247
it's not going to be long before
there's a Democratic president

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:51.917
who does the same thing in
regards to what, climate change.

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.486
-That's what
you're worried about?

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.055
That's like saying, "I would
give this homeless guy a dollar,

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.757
but you know
he's just going to use it

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.859
to print out his résumé
and find a job."

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.561
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.130
There's a big difference between
the border and climate change.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.798
Climate change
is an actual emergency.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:08.101
And we can't build a wall
to stop it,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.803
unless we build one
around the entire planet.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.139
"We're going to build
a space wall, folks,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.874
and Mars is going to
pay for it."

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.208
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:18.645
In fact, climate change
is such a serious emergency

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:21.580
that last year, after a summer
of heat waves and wildfires,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.283
scientists issued
a dire warning.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.586
We have just 12 years to limit
devastating global warning.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.688
One scientist said,
"It's like a deafening,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.890
piercing smoke alarm
going off in the kitchen.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.692
We have to put out the fire."

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.960
And another said it's like
a speeding freight train.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.295
And you know it's bad,

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.397
because scientists try not
to use language like that.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.834
The last time a scientist
freaked out like that,

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.901
he was trapped
in the Temple of Doom.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:46.505
-We are going to die!

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.508
-Now, in response to that,
a reasonable person might say,

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:51.110
"What can we do to stop this?"

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.913
Instead we have a President who
thinks you can stop wildfires

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.681
not by slowing down
climate change,

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.950
but by raking leaves
in the forest.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.686
That's what he told Fox News
last year

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.287
even after he was asked
point-blank

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.822
about the role
of climate change.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.791
-I was watching the firemen
the other day,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.793
and they were raking areas.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.528
They were raking areas.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:11.664
Where the fire was right over
there, and they're raking trees,

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.633
little trees like this that
are -- not trees, little bushes

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:16.569
that you could see
are totally dry.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.138
Weeds.
And they're raking them.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.507
They're on fire.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:22.141
That should have been
all raked out.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:24.243
-What about the argument --
-You wouldn't have the fires.

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:26.145
-What about the argument
it's climate change?

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:28.314
That it's drier, it's hotter,

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.083
and that that's
contributing to it?

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.751
-Maybe it contributes
a little bit.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.387
The big problem we have
is management.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.156
When I was in a certain state --
I won't say which --

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.492
the governor said,
"You know, we've tested it.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.859
We clean out areas,

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:43.662
and we actually set the fire
just to see.

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:45.665
We lose almost nothing."

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.167
-Why won't you say
which state it was?

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.268
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.137
Seems to me
if a governor figured out

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.972
how to stop forest fires
with a rake,

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.841
they'd want their name
out there.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:58.311
Is it because they're from
Nev-a-happened-a?

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.379
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:01.680
So if you're a lawmaker

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.516
faced with the dire warnings
of climate scientists,

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:05.718
you have two options.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.453
You can put more money
into raking little trees,

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.221
or you can radically
overhaul the economy

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:10.790
in a way that would help
stave off disaster.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.358
And that's the path
some Democrats,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:17.130
led by Congresswoman
Alexandra Ocasio-Cortez, chose

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.400
when they unveiled a plan called
the Green New Deal,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.869
which envisions
a 10-year economic mobilization

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.670
that would phase out
fossil fuel use

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.338
and overhaul
the nation's infrastructure.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:27.573
The plan has been endorsed

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.808
by several Democratic candidates
for president

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:31.044
but slammed by Republicans

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.312
and former Starbucks CEO
Howard Schultz.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:36.382
Last week, Schultz said the
Green New Deal is not realistic.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.550
Schultz has been threatening
to run as an independent

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.319
unless the Democrats
nominate a moderate.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.388
Yesterday after he announced
his own bid,

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.291
Bernie Sanders was asked
about Schultz's threat on CBS

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.826
and didn't seem
to take it seriously.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.528
-Howard Schultz has now said he
would not run as an independent

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:52.130
if the Democrats nominate
a moderate.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.533
-Oh, isn't that nice?

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:56.736
Why is Howard Schultz
on every television station

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.804
in this country?

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.872
Why are you quoting
Howard Schultz?

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.273
Because he's a billionaire.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:04.877
-You're asking Bernie what
he thinks about a billionaire?

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.146
That just makes you look
like a bad journalist.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.948
If you know one thing
about Bernie,

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.450
it's how he feels
about billionaires.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:16.021
His Ben &amp; Jerry's flavor is
called Tax All the Billionaires.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:17.857
It's not even an ice cream pun.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.827
It's just vanilla and nickels.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:26.232
The Green New Deal is just
a framework, resolution

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.633
that sets out a series of goals,

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.668
and it also tries
a novel political strategy.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.704
Rather than just address climate
on its own,

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.940
the bill combines environmental
issues with economic ones,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.408
like guaranteeing a job and
healthcare to every American.

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:37.676
Those are bold proposals,

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.812
and anyone can debate them
on the merits.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.480
But as fact checkers have noted,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:45.451
no one is proposing to eliminate
all planes, cars, cows,

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.052
oil, gas, and the military.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.654
And yet that hasn't
stopped Trump

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.256
from repeating those lies
anyway.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.158
-I think it is very important
for the Democrats

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.926
to press forward
with their Green New Deal.

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:56.362
It would be great for
the so-called carbon footprint

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.898
to permanently eliminate
all planes, cars, cows,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.499
oil, gas, and the military,

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.568
even if no other country
would do the same.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.003
Brilliant!

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:07.674
-I really don't like their
policy of taking away your car,

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:10.376
of taking away
your airplane flights,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.680
of, "Let's hop a train
to California,"

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.980
of...

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.082
[ Booing ]

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.451
You're not allowed
to own cows anymore.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.986
You know, a lot of problems.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.755
-Man, Trump is getting
really desperate.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:23.923
In two years, he's gone from,

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.591
"They're going to
take your guns away,"

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:28.327
to, "They're going to
take your cows away."

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:31.030
No one is outlawing cows.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.233
You know what we call that?
Fake moos.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.202
-Fake moos!

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.903
[ Air horn blows ]

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.972
[ Mooing ]

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.774
[ Applause ]

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:46.211
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:47.713
-Trump has basically
cycled through

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.415
one mode of transportation
after another

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.450
and falsely claimed
that the Green New Deal

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.451
would eliminate it.

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:53.919
For example, the Green New Deal

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.188
would prioritize investment
in high-speed rail

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.524
with the hope that it would
reduce our reliance

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.093
on short-distance air travel,
not eliminate it.

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:02.461
But Trump lied about that, too.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.163
-It would shut down
American energy,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.965
which I don't think
the people in Texas

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.366
are going to be happy with that.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:10.670
[ Booing ]

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:14.773
It would shut down a little
thing called air travel.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:17.676
[ Booing ]

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.445
-Of course, those weren't boos.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:22.047
People just brought their cows
to the rally.

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:24.683
"You're not safe at home,
Bessie!

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:26.352
The government's
coming to get you.

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:29.655
You got to come to the rally!"

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:33.459
Nobody is outlawing cars or cows
or anything, for that matter.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:36.496
The basic premise is that
government can help spur change

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:39.065
by making renewable technologies
more efficient

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.467
and thus more affordable and
more attractive to consumers.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.835
But Trump is, of course,

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.803
not interested in engaging
with any of those specifics.

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:47.640
He'd rather make fun of the name
of the Green New Deal.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:52.411
-Last week, they introduced
a massive government takeover

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:55.914
that would destroy
our incredible economic gains.

00:06:55.914 --> 00:07:00.085
They introduced
the so-called Green New Deal.

00:07:00.085 --> 00:07:02.188
[ Booing ]

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:14.033
It sounds like a high school
term paper that got a low mark.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:17.736
-I'm not sure I'd be making fun
of bad grades if I were you.

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:21.007
I'm pretty sure you're the only
guy Clippy ever gave up on.

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:23.576
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:27.713
Republicans have manufactured a
fake emergency over immigration

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:29.582
and now they're worried
a Democrat will come along

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.450
and declare a real emergency
over climate change.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.919
And instead of debating the
Green New Deal on its merits,

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:35.787
they're making up lies
about its content.

00:07:35.787 --> 00:07:37.823
But polls show most people
aren't buying it.

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:40.026
When Republicans whine
about the Green New Deal,

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:41.026
most voters say...

00:07:41.026 --> 00:07:42.828
-Isn't that nice?

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:44.497
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.399
[ Cheers and applause ]

